    survivingLiens: "A California tax deed conveys free of most liens existing before the sale, but federal tax liens survive (the IRS keeps a 120-day post-sale redemption right), as do taxes/assessments that become payable after the sale. County materials also note public liens (e.g. improvement bonds, demolition liens) may not always be discharged — verify R&T Code §3712 exceptions parcel-by-parcel.",
