    survivingLiens: "Hawaiʻi county tax deeds generally cut off many junior private liens after proper sale, but federal tax liens and some governmental assessments can survive. Always run full title; island-specific water, shoreline, and SMA issues are separate from tax liens.",
    quietTitle: "Practically often required for insurable title after a Hawaiʻi tax deed, especially before resale or financing.",
