    notes: "Montana tax-lien assignment county with a separate tax-deed auction channel. Missoula County Clerk & Treasurer attaches statutory tax liens on delinquent real property (typically first business day in August; $75 tax lien certificate fee). Third-party investors may request assignment of outstanding liens in late August under a published priority policy (MCA §15-17-323) — this is assignment/OTC, not a competitive live lien auction. After the multi-year redemption window, the county has offered tax-deeded parcels via Bid4Assets online auctions (e.g. Nov 2025 cycle with deposit deadline and full-payment settlement rules). Confirm current-year assignment instructions and any 2026 Bid4Assets tax-deed sale on missoulacounty.gov and Bid4Assets. Hire counsel before investing in MT liens.",
