    survivingLiens: "At the certificate stage the buyer holds a lien, not clear title — owner redemption extinguishes the certificate. Other encumbrances remain; tax liens take priority but do not extinguish covenants or easements. After a tax deed issues following foreclosure, most private liens are cut off, but federal tax liens (IRS 120-day post-sale redemption) and some governmental assessments can survive.",
