    survivingLiens: "Upset sale deeds often leave mortgages and other liens intact — read Upset vs Judicial carefully. Judicial (free-and-clear) after proper lienholder notice typically cuts off most junior private liens; federal and some state liens can survive. Repository sales follow Bureau terms.",
    quietTitle: "Quiet title or extended seasoning often required for insurable resale after Upset; Judicial improves marketability but title insurers still underwrite carefully.",
    gisMap: { label: "Indiana County Assessment / GIS parcel resources", url: "https://www.indianacountypa.gov/departments/tax-assessment/" },
